# README current build link

Whenever `__version__` changes (or docs mention the package version), update
`README.md` so GitHub visitors always get a download link for the current build:

1. Set **Version:** to match `src/eq_augs/__init__.py` `__version__`.
2. Set **Current build:** to a direct download that uses that same version:

```markdown
**Version:** X.Y.Z
**Current build:** [EQAugs-X.Y.Z.exe](https://github.com/Neclub/EQ-Augs/releases/latest/download/EQAugs-X.Y.Z.exe)
([all releases](https://github.com/Neclub/EQ-Augs/releases/latest))
```

3. Keep the local build path example (`dist\EQAugs-X.Y.Z.exe`) on the same version.
4. Keep `MERGE_NOTES.md` standalone version strings aligned when bumping.

Do not remove the **Current build** link from the README.
